            <ArticleTitle>Portal vein aneurysm and portal biliopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>658</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/jhbp.383</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Highlight Kurtcehajic and colleagues present a rare case of congenital portal vein aneurysm (PVA) with biliopathy. Symptoms associated with PVA occur in less than 10% of cases. Imaging modalities showed the PVA partially compressing the common and right hepatic ducts. Conservative treatment markedly lowered bilirubin levels and relieved the abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
